module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**bare name resolved by proximity, standing in for resolution** (the reference-edge reader in `v1_compiler.cli_run` `entry_resolve` binds a bare name in an IMPORT-LESS file by 'proximity disambiguation' -- the longest shared module-path prefix with a pool declarer -- yielding a UniqueBare or AmbiguousBare edge. A heuristic standing where lexical resolution (locals plus imports) is the authority; DESIGN §4: in a closed system a heuristic is never necessary.)",

    "INVALID STATE: a dependency edge from a module to a declarer it does not lexically bind. The edge widens closures and affected-set selection and can name a homonym the source never meant, silently, with no refusal.",

    "SPECIMEN (gunbc#13526, open when this row was written): a supplied fixture declaring a homonym `Present` beside `std.optional { Present }` produced an edge from an importer of `std.optional` to the homonym's module while the reader still resolved by proximity. #13526 closed the arm for import-BEARING files (bare names there are lexically bound, only qualified chains become edges) and kept the proximity tier for import-less files only.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT (gunbc#13533): silent wrongness on the import-less UniqueBare path, outside the ladder. Import-bearing files were already closed by #13526.",

    "EVIDENCE, EXECUTED (gunbc#13579): two populations, not one. (a) Longest-common-prefix ranking among homonyms -- RED `cli_run` `reference_edge_producer_tests` `proximity_must_not_bind_an_importless_bare_name_to_a_sibling_homonym` over the real `dependency_resolution_facts` union. Fixture: `frontier.child.consumer` calls `duplicated()`; `frontier` and `frontier.child.plant` both declare it. RED captured on the merge-base ranking (entry_resolve.rs identical at 17ebbde83b and 82a3edfea3): `proximity UniqueBare bound the sibling plant: [\"frontier.child.plant\"]`. After the climb that test is the producer regression control; positive `an_importless_bare_name_on_the_ancestor_chain_still_resolves`. (b) Census-unique off-chain UniqueBinding -- `unique_off_chain_bare_name_compiles_and_keeps_its_uniquebare_edge` proves `test.user` can call `test.decl.shared_fn` with no import and no ancestor, and the producer keeps UniqueBare because UniqueBinding still accepts. Two off-chain homonyms: `off_chain_homonym_with_no_lexical_binder_is_refused_on_the_resolve_path` runs `compile_sources` over `load_sources_for_entry_with_pool` (not `resolve_entry_with_index`) and asserts blocking compile failure containing `function 'shared' not found in scope`; it is not a typed-and-located diagnostic identity. Live dag+src/v2 UniqueBare identity is unchanged (gunbc#13579).",

    "RUNG NOW: (a) longest-common-prefix ranking among homonyms is mechanically preventable (rung 2) on the UniqueBare producer -- the RED is the producer's edge set. (b) census-unique off-chain GlobalBareUniqueBinding remains OUTSIDE the lexical guarantee; `pick_importless_bare`'s `mods.len() == 1` arm is not a lexical-scope proof, and `global_bare_lookup_candidates` UniqueBinding does not check the ancestor chain. Those UniqueBare edges stay in the reader until canonical acceptance and edge derivation change together -- dropping them from the reader alone would undercount an accepted call. The row's minimum is (b), not 2. A written import is a legitimate lexical binding even when its target is not an ancestor -- the guarantee forbids bindings without lexical authority, not off-chain references in general. CEILING 3 at source -> accepted graph. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: GlobalBareUniqueBinding of a name with no lexical authority is refused, and this producer stops emitting UniqueBare for that case in the same change.",

    "CLIMB, (b) (node://adhoc-5fdefc60-2eb, found by bright-crane-219 on gunbc#15230 via a 3-file probe: a type and a `data` declared once in A, referenced bare in B that never imports A, accepted with zero diagnostics -- it made unimported names in `test.claim.gcp_iam_bootstrap_population_split_witness` execute green). RED `unimported_bare_name_floor_test` `unimported_bare_type_reference_refuses` and `unimported_bare_data_value_reference_refuses`, positive controls `imported_bare_reference_compiles_clean`, `chain_ancestor_bare_reference_compiles_clean`, `kernel_builtins_and_none_stay_bare_and_admitted`. Earliest unjustified boundary: the UNIQUE arm of the seed's global-bare pool (`global_bare_lookup_candidates`, `borrowed_census_decl`) answered from any module while the homonym arm already applied the chain test under NamespaceOnlyY; one shared `global_bare_declarer_in_scope` now gates both name-resolution sites, and `pick_importless_bare` stops emitting UniqueBare for an off-chain declarer in the same change. By-identity and owner-perspective lookups (`declaration_node_of_ref`, `declaration_binding_of_ref`, `global_bare_owner_module`, `declaration_named_by_type_name`) are not name-resolution sites (they take an already-resolved reference or qualify from the owner's view) and stay ungated. v2 native: the atom door has no pool (#12048); the surviving v2 pool consumers (`resolve_pattern_atom_names_constructor`, `resolve_declared_payload_path_lookup`, `resolution_provenance`) are separate paths not changed here and remain the minimum for the v2 route until read.",

    "RUNG HONESTY (gunbc#15247): the discriminating RED and its controls run only as v1 unit tests (`v1-compiler-tests` `unimported_bare_name_floor_test`; positive control `imported_bare_reference_compiles_clean`), not on the required `v2-bootstrap` path. Whole-corpus evidence is the non-required heal job. The seed-side class sits at mechanically preventable, not enrolled on the required path. Climb trigger: a row of `gunbc.emitted_subject_build_gate` judged by the self-host/native gate that refuses an unimported bare name. The v2-side pool consumers stay open as above. The legacy ImportScoped policy arm was deleted from the gate (`global_bare_declarer_in_scope`); the policy cell itself retires with namespace-resolution-design section 13 step 4.",

    "REVIEW TELL: a reader or resolver that ranks candidate declarers by path similarity, shared prefix or 'closest' instead of refusing; an edge whose only justification is that one pool declarer exists.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
